## Next {id="nm-roadmap-next"}

Ordered by how much each would matter in an enterprise evaluation
(`docs/status-2026-09-25.md` §5), plus the items `PLAN.md` §23.22 step 4
leaves open.

| Item | Why | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Multi-node collaboration fan-out for the Yjs relay (Redis or Postgres `LISTEN/NOTIFY`, keep persist-before-ack) | Today multi-node needs sticky routing per document | status §5 #1 |
| Same-block concurrent edits (character-level Yjs text inside a block) | Two people editing one paragraph keep both versions | status §5 #2 |
| PostgreSQL as the Cloud datastore | Cloud runs on SQLite; only DDL exists for Postgres | `docs/enterprise.noma`, `PLAN.md` §23.22 step 4 |
| Native SAML | Some IdPs are SAML-only; today SAML goes through a trusted-header proxy | status §5 #3, `docs/enterprise.noma` |
| Embedding score calibration per provider | Thresholds were tuned for hash vectors | status §5 #4 |
| Instance-role S3 credentials and `noma cloud migrate-blobs` | Run on AWS without static keys | status §5 #6 |
| OIDC logout, group sync, multiple IdPs | Enterprise identity depth | status §5 #7 |
| Real AWS/EU staging deployment with a smoke test | CloudFormation is validated, never deployed | status §5 #8, `docs/review-2026-09.md` status update |
| Third-party pentest report | Only the in-repo review pack exists | `docs/enterprise.noma` |
| Webhooks for standalone pages | They fire only for pages inside spaces | `docs/review-2026-09.md` status update |

