## Dogfooding {id="nm-roadmap-dogfooding"}

Noma Cloud now runs **self-hosted on a home mini PC**, with **one space per
project**: Noma, EZKeel, Stratos, and OrgFlow. Each space is synced from
that repository's `wiki/` directory (this page lives at
`wiki/noma/roadmap.noma`). The deployment kit is `deploy/minipc/`; see the
Operations page (`wiki/noma/operations.noma`).

::callout{tone="warning"}
This is a single home host. Treat it as a technical preview: backups and a
restore rehearsal come before anyone relies on it (`docs/runbooks/cloud-launch.md`,
"Backup and restore").
::

What dogfooding should validate:

| Area | What to check | Done when |
|---|---|---|
| Wiki editing + Git round-trip | Edit in the Visual editor and in source; run `noma cloud sync` against each repo's `wiki/`; conflicts produce `.noma.conflict` files | A week of edits with no lost change and byte-identical round-trips |
| Agent proof → approve → apply | An agent proposes block patches; a different human approves; a stale `baseHash` is refused | At least one real agent change applied per space |
| Work issues | Plan real work as issues; chat message → issue; inline page tasks | Day-to-day tasks tracked in Work, not elsewhere |
| Chat | Project and topic channels; threads saved as `.noma` pages; agents answering mentions | One decision captured from a thread into a page |
| `/deploy` and `/test` via ezkeel | Runs start from a thread, need approval when an agent asks, post results back, move issues | A green run moves an issue to review; a red test files a follow-up |
| Search and Ask | ⌘K across pages, issues, chat; Ask returns block-level citations or abstains | Failed searches and wrong answers are logged as issues |

::decision{id="nm-dogfood-feedback-loop" status="proposed" owner="maintainer"}
Every friction found while dogfooding becomes a **Work issue labelled
`dogfood`** in the affected project's space, filed the same day, with the
page or channel link and what was expected. Triage the `dogfood` label
weekly; fixes that change behaviour get a `CHANGELOG.md` entry.
::

## Decisions {id="nm-roadmap-decisions"}

Accepted decisions live in `docs/direction.noma`; they are summarized here.

::decision{id="nm-dec-wiki-direction" status="accepted" owner="maintainer"}
Noma is the wiki for the agentic-AI era; the format and Noma Cloud are one
product (2026-09-23). Source: `docs/direction.noma` `wiki-direction`,
`PLAN.md` §23.19.
::

::decision{id="nm-dec-collaboration-surface" status="accepted" owner="maintainer"}
Noma grows into one collaboration surface: wiki, Work, Chat, and run
environments on ezkeel. Chat must always land in source (2026-09-26).
Source: `docs/direction.noma` `collaboration-surface`, `PLAN.md` §23.21.
::

::decision{id="nm-dec-lego" status="accepted" owner="maintainer"}
`.noma` is the standard; HTML is a projection and a sandboxed escape hatch.
Per-space style-token vocabularies, sandboxed `::html` widgets in Cloud,
PaperDOM forked in-repo (2026-09-24). Source: `docs/strategy-2026-09.md` §8.
::

::decision{id="nm-dec-next-release-version" status="open" owner="maintainer"}
Version number and headline for the release that ships the `[Unreleased]`
work. Not decided as of 2026-09-27.
::

## Risks {id="nm-roadmap-risks"}

::risk{id="nm-risk-scope" severity="high" owner="maintainer"}
Scope sprawl. The review found Cloud, enterprise, and PaperDOM at about 40%
of `src/` with little depth where users spend time. Four product surfaces
now share one repo. Mitigation: dogfood, and prefer depth fixes from
`dogfood` issues over new surfaces. Source: `docs/review-2026-09.md` §1.
::

::risk{id="nm-risk-scale" severity="medium" owner="maintainer"}
Single-node limits. SQLite datastore and single-process Yjs fan-out mean
one host per workspace. Fine for dogfooding, blocks larger deployments.
Source: `docs/status-2026-09-25.md` §5, `docs/enterprise.noma`.
::

::risk{id="nm-risk-unreleased" severity="medium" owner="maintainer"}
A large body of merged work is unreleased and only tested in CI. Bugs will
surface first in dogfooding. Source: `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`.
::

::risk{id="nm-risk-same-block" severity="medium" owner="maintainer"}
Same-block concurrent edits keep both versions instead of merging, which
can look like data duplication to users. Source: `docs/status-2026-09-25.md` §5 #2.
::

::risk{id="nm-risk-runs" severity="medium" owner="maintainer"}
`/deploy` and `/test` start real workloads on ezkeel. Guardrails exist
(owner opt-in, minutes budget, concurrency cap, `run` capability, approval
by a different person), but have not been exercised outside tests.
Source: `docs/noma-cloud.noma` "Code, CI, and run environments".
::

::risk{id="nm-risk-v1" severity="low" owner="maintainer"}
v1.0 needs an external consumer and an out-of-repo second implementation;
neither exists yet. Source: `PLAN.md` §25.3.
::

## Agent follow-ups {id="nm-roadmap-agent-tasks"}

::agent_task{id="nm-task-wiki-sync-check" scope="wiki"}
After each merge to `main`, compare `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` and
`PLAN.md` §24 with this page and the space home. Propose block patches (by
`nm-` ID) for anything that moved between Now, Next, and shipped. Do not
rewrite whole pages.
::

::agent_task{id="nm-task-dogfood-triage" scope="work"}
Weekly: list open Work issues labelled `dogfood` across the four spaces,
group them by area (wiki, agents, Work, Chat, runs, search), and post a
digest in the Noma space's topic channel.
::

::agent_task{id="nm-task-status-gaps" scope="docs"}
When a gap from `docs/status-2026-09-25.md` §5 ships, propose moving its
row from Next to shipped here and check that `docs/enterprise.noma` says
the same.
::
